{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["What size of request should go through this form, and what is small enough to just ask for?","Which constraints matter most in your organisation, such as data protection or accessibility?","Who decides which requests are built, and how often do they meet?","Should the form ask for a budget holder or sponsor?"],"howToUseResponses":"Read the problem and the current workaround before the proposed solution, because the right fix is often smaller than the request. Follow up with the requester to turn the must-have list into acceptance criteria before estimating. Score requests by the difference they would make against the number of users and any fixed deadline, and export the list to CSV to review it with whoever sets priorities.","customizeSteps":["Replace the constraints list with the checks your team has to make, such as security review or accessibility.","Name your internal systems in a dropdown if requests always touch the same few.","Share the link where requests currently arrive, and add your review cadence to the ending so requesters know when to expect an answer."],"faqs":[{"q":"What should a software development request include?","a":"The problem, who has it, how it is handled today, what the solution must do and any constraints or deadlines. That is enough for a developer to ask sensible questions and give a rough estimate."},{"q":"Why ask for the problem instead of the solution?","a":"People often ask for the first fix they thought of. Knowing the underlying problem lets the team suggest something simpler, or something that already exists."},{"q":"Is this the same as a feature request form?","a":"It overlaps. A feature request usually comes from customers about a product; this form is for internal teams asking for tools, changes or integrations, and gathers more detail for estimating."},{"q":"Can I add technical questions?","a":"Yes. Copy it with Use this template and add questions about platforms, data sources or hosting. You can also branch so only technical requesters see them."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":10,"title":"Software development request","description":"Take requests for new tools and features, starting from the problem rather than the solution.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_software00","ref":"welcome","title":"Have something you'd like built or changed? Start with the problem and we'll work out the solution together.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"buttonLabel":"Start","type":"welcome"},{"id":"blk_software01","ref":"requester","title":"Who is making the request?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"contact_info","fields":["first_name","last_name","email"]},{"id":"blk_software02","ref":"team","title":"Which team or department are you in?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"short_text","unique":false,"minLength":0,"maxLength":150},{"id":"blk_software03","ref":"kind","title":"What kind of request is this?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_a_new_tool","label":"A new tool or app","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_a_new_feature","label":"A new feature in an existing system","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_a_change_to","label":"A change to how something works","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_connecting_two_systems","label":"Connecting two systems","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_a_report_or","label":"A report or data export","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_software04","ref":"existing_system","title":"Which existing system or systems does it involve?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"short_text","unique":false,"minLength":0,"maxLength":200},{"id":"blk_software05","ref":"problem","title":"What problem are you trying to solve?","description":"Describe the problem, not the solution. 